hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1127","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, Yahya bin Sa’id told us, and Sa’id bin Abi Arouba also read to us from his book, and Bundar also told us, It was narrated to us by Ibn Abi Adi, on the authority of Sa’id, H. Harun bin Ishaq Al-Hamdani narrated to us, it was narrated to us by Abdah, on the authority of Sa’id, H. It was narrated to us by Bundar, Muadh bin Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, H, and Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Muhammad bin Sawa narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed, all of them, on the authority of Qatada, On the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, he said: I came to Hakim bin Aflah, and he and I went to Aisha, may God be pleased with her. On her behalf, we asked for permission, so we entered upon her and said: O Mother of the Believers, inform me about the character of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: “Have you not read the Qur’an?” meaning his saying, “Indeed, you are of great character.” Surah Al-Qalam, verse 4. He said: Yes. She said: “For the character of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace It was the Qur’an.” So I said: “O Mother of the Believers, inform me about the rise of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” She said: “Do you not recite this Surah? O you, Muzzammil.” He said: So I said: Yes, she said: “For God enjoined the standing at the beginning of this Surah, so the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up.” And his companions perplexed, until their feet swelled, and the end of it remained for twelve months in heaven, then God sent down relief at the end of this. Surah, so the night prayer became voluntary after an obligatory prayer.” Then they mentioned the hadith, and at the end of the hadith, he said: So I went to Ibn Abbas and informed him. With her speech, he said: She spoke the truth"
